{
  "format": 2,
  "id": "frontier",
  "name": "Frontier",
  "description": "A small, dry ensemble for the valley in the wary-frontier manner. The voice is a plucked zither, VCSL's dan tranh, bent and scooped like a dulcimer played by someone listening over their shoulder. Under it a pizzicato walk in 7/8, a Virtual Playing Orchestra upright bass doubled an octave up by plucked cellos, limps along with the zither, and the cello section holds a low drone. As the music's intensity rises, violas take an answering line and a kalimba ticks in the long group of the bar; at the top, the VCSL ritual kit's frame drums and slit drums fill out the limp, timpani mark the downbeats and the drone goes to tremolo. A room rather than a hall, so the valley sounds open and close at once.",
